\par Dear Colleagues \endash  
\par                               Herewith the Third Circular, a little earlier than anticipated, in order to confirm that the \lquote early bird\rquote 
 discounted registration ended (as advertised) on May 30th.  The registration fee for delegates that are not full-time students is therefore \'a339 (which is still lower than the registration fee for the last two years \endash  what a bargain!).  
\par 
\par As most of you know, the deadline for applications to the Jones-Fenleigh Memorial Fund and the deadline for the submission of abstracts (see Second Circular for format guidelines) was announced originally as Friday 15}{\super th}{
 June.  My thanks to those of you  who have managed to conform to those deadlines.  However, I have been reminded that early approaches from some of you (just after the First 
Circular went out at the start of March) led to my indicating the likely deadlines as being the end of June.  I am bound to honour that, and so for reasons of fairness the deadline for both abstracts and JFMF applications has been extended to the end of J
une \endash  in other words, midnight on Saturday 30}{\super th}{
.  A provisional list of contributions will be issued thereafter as part of the Fourth Circular.  The abstracts will be subject to editing by the organisers (following external review) for the abstracts volume to be produced for the conference pack.

\par 
\par The pleasant news is that the refurbished Hunterian Museum did (eventually) reopen for its bicentenary, so I can present to you the following provisional schedule for the week of the symposium:
