\par }{\b {\*\bkmkstart OLE_LINK4}Registered delegates}{: you will shortly receive an e-mail that will indicate what stage your attendance processing is at \endash 
 for example, whether we have received an abstract from you, how much money is still outstanding on your account.  Please check that all the details that you receive in that e-mail concur with what you believe to be the case \endash 
 and respond indicating when you expect any outstanding matters to be resolved.
\par 
\par }{\b Presentation format}{: it will be expected that your presentation will be in PowerPoint.  In this regard a
ll versions created in PowerPoint from 2000 to XP are supported, whether created on Mac or PC.  If you have any special requirements beyond this (overhead projector, slide projector, other format of presentation tool), please let me know.  You are urged t
o send a CD of your presentation in advance of the meeting (as this will be the only way to ensure compatibility of your presentation with our set-up), and to bring a further CD or memory stick version with you as insurance.
\par 
\par As the language of the meeting will be English, any delegate whose first language is not English should let the organisers know, as linguistic assistance may be available.
\par 
\par The deadline for accommodation bookings is Wednesday 4}{\super th}{ July.  Any applications received after that date will be liable to a handling surcharge (as the rooming list for everyone else will already have gone to the accommodation service).
\par 
\par If you are intending to stay on beyond the conference or arrive early for collections study or other reasons, then please let me know as soon as possible so that it can be determined whether or not accommodation can be set aside for you.
\par 
\par }{\b Computer access}{: As noted in the previous circular, internet access will be possible from your room in the Queen Margaret residence \endash  all you have t
o do is bring a laptop and connection cable (an RJ45 network cable, for the geeks out there).  
\par 
\par For those wanting to check e-mail without bringing a laptop, there are plenty of internet caf\'e9 facilities around the campus.
\par 
\par }{\b Disabled access}{: A point that I should have made clear in the First Circular - just to reassure all delegates that lecture theatres and reception venues have disabled access.
\par 
\par }{\b Parking}{: Please notify me if you will be bringing a vehicle and so will require parking at the residence.
\par 
\par }{\b Payment}{: In order to qualify for the early registration discount, payment must be received by the end of July.  Payments received after this date will default to the full registration fee.  All payments }{\b MUST}{
 be received by the Friday 27th July, in order to process accommodation and other hospitality fees prior to the start of the meeting.  Recent changes to the University of Glasgow\rquote 
s accounts procedure have made it necessary to alter the financial arrangements for delegate payment for SVPCA this year.  This means that BACS/direct transfer and PayPal payments can be received, but credit card payments cannot be accepted.  
\par 
\par }{\b Poster Boards}{: Guideline approximate dimensions are being provided for poster production, to enable the best use of poster-board space \endash 
 please attempt to format your poster to comply with one of these options, so that we can guarantee you a space.  For portrait format, size options are 60cm x 90cm, 90cm x 120cm, 75cm x 120cm.  For landscape format, size options are 120cm x 90cm
, 120cm x 60cm, 90cm x 60cm. 
\par 
\par }{\b Fourth Circular}{: To be issued in July with details of field trip, orientation maps (including final venue for Icebreaker), and a provisional list of speakers.{\*\bkmkend OLE_LINK4}
\par }}